{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-b51fed1f21e1c30a", "type": "tool_result", "content": "400\tTwelve metrics in three pillars, no composite; Table 11 fixes every name, symbol and range, and\n401\tAppendix H gives the definitions and formulas.\n402\tMetrics are computed per run and averaged; worlds\n403\tare pooled by unweighted mean over equal-sized\n404\tcells; J• denotes an LLM judge (Table 12). The\n405\tsuite is one evaluation system, not twelve scripts:\n406\ta single pipeline computes every metric in every\n407\tworld from the same three artefacts (the merged\n408\ttranscript, the simulation tick stream and the isolated agent audio) under one configuration, one\n409\tjudge set and one bootstrap procedure.\n410\tConversational dynamics. Turn-taking (TT)\n411\tscores every floor transfer’s offset on an on-time\n412\tcurve chosen by the transfer’s kind, and a single\n413\tunanswered user turn zeroes the conversation; it is\n414\tported verbatim from EVA-Bench (Bogavelli et al.,\n415\t2026) and is the one metric in the suite where silence is penalised rather than rewarded. Conversation progression (CP) is one topic-free judge pass\n416\tover the transcript. Selectivity (SEL) is the fraction of injected distractor events correctly ignored,\n417\tscored against gold labels written at injection time.\n418\tAll three read only the transcript and timing log, so\n419\tidentical code runs in every world.\n420\tAgentic capability. The goal-state check GS\n421\tasks whether the world ended in the right state:\n422\ta canonical hash of the record store against a gold\n423\treplay, and in Pathfinding the walker’s final position against the destination. The reward multiplies\n424\t\n425\t\fexactly the binary factors each scenario names (GS,\n426\ta gold-action match ACT, and, where what is said\n427\tor refused is the point, a judged assertion NLA); in\n428\tPathfinding, which has no gold action list, an efficiency conjunct (η ≥ 0.75) replaces them so that\n429\tarrival alone is not enough. Pass@1 is the mean\n430\tsingle-run reward, Pass@3 the at-least-once reward\n431\tover three draws, and Pass3 τ -bench’s Passk at\n432\tk = 3 (Yao et al., 2024); Appendix H gives the\n433\testimators. Effort is measured against each task’s\n434\town reference workload: the over-effort ratio ϱ+\n435\tand the under-effort share π − , each reported with\n436\tits conditioning share. A system that never acts\n437\tscores near-perfect selectivity and competitive turntaking, so experience metrics are read jointly with\n438\tπ − ; a null reference policy ships with the release\n439\tas a constructive check.\n440\tNaturalness. Faithfulness (FAI) is one judge\n441\tpass over the transcript with the agent’s instructions, role and tool schemas, five binary dimensions\n442\tscored as their minimum. DNSMOS (Reddy et al.,\n443\t2022), UTMOS (Saeki et al., 2022) and NISQA\n444\t(Mittag et al., 2021) are no-reference MOS predictors over the isolated agent channel.\n445\t\n446\t5\n447\t\n448\tResults and Discussion\n449\t\n450\tTable 3 carries the full suite less the effort pair; Table 4 carries the effort pair. We read the results in\n451\tthree passes: what the main table says about each\n452\tcapability pillar and how the pillars relate (Section 5.1), how the systems fail (Section 5.2), and\n453\twhat the auxiliary instruments separate that headline metrics cannot (Section 5.3). The remaining\n454\tanalyses (the deep dives, the range analysis, the\n455\tmetric–reward associations, and the harness dials)\n456\tare in Appendices I–L.\n457\t5.1\n458\t\n459\tThree capabilities, one table\n460\t\n461\tTable 3 asks three questions of the same five systems: did the task get done (Agentic Capability),\n462\thow did the conversation go (Conversational Dynamics), and how did it sound (Naturalness). To\n463\tour knowledge this is the first evaluation to score\n464\tall three side by side for full-duplex voice agents,\n465\tso the table is also a first answer to whether they\n466\ttravel together. On the agentic pillar the all six rows\n467\torder the systems cleanly: Grok Voice Think\n468\tFast 1.0 leads (Pass@1 0.490, GS 0.779), GPTRealtime-2.1 follows (0.433), Gemini-3.1-FlashLive is third (0.398), GPT-Realtime-2.1-mini\n469\tcompletes less than half of what its full-size sibling\n470\t\n471\tdoes (0.188), and Nova 2 Sonic barely registers\n472\t(0.011). The level is a property of the world as\n473\tmuch as of the system: GPT-Realtime-2.1 alone\n474\tspans 0.200 in Banking to 0.674 in Travel,\n475\tworlds that differ only in subject matter, while\n476\tthe ordering barely moves (Appendix J). Reliability decays fast: Pass3 is roughly half of Pass@1\n477\tfor the two leaders and under a third for GPTRealtime-2.1-mini, and Figure 1 shows the same\n478\tdecay at every k; no system passes even one scenario in five reliably. Conversational Dynamics\n479\tdoes not reproduce that order. GPT-Realtime-2.1\n480\tholds the best turn-taking (0.653 pooled), Grok\n481\tVoice Think Fast 1.0 the best conversation progression (1.814), and Gemini-3.1-Flash-Live, third\n482\ton the reward, is last on turn-taking (0.388) because it pauses to call tools. Nova 2 Sonic is\n483\tthe sharpest dissociation in the table: respectable\n484\tturn-taking (0.566) and the best selectivity in every\n485\tworld (0.960–0.995) sit beside an agentic column\n486\tof near-zeros. Being good in the conversation and\n487\tbeing good at the task are different capabilities, a\n488\tsystem can hold the floor gracefully while doing\n489\tnothing, and a leaderboard built on dynamics alone\n490\twould rank the least capable system near the top.\n491\tNaturalness separates least. All five systems sit\n492\twithin a quarter point on DNSMOS (3.13–3.40),\n493\tand the two MOS leaders, GPT-Realtime-2.1 and\n494\tGPT-Realtime-2.1-mini, differ by 2.3× on the\n495\treward: how a system sounds carries almost no\n496\tinformation about what it completes. We read this\n497\ttwo ways. Production systems have largely converged on acoustic quality, so this pillar now needs\n498\tsharper instruments, expressiveness, empathy and\n499\tprosodic appropriateness rather than signal quality. And a deployment decision made on perceived\n500\tquality alone will pick the wrong system; faithfulness (FAI), judged from content rather than sound,\n501\tis the one naturalness column that still tracks the\n502\treward.\n503\t5.2\n504\t\n505\tFailure modes across the worlds\n506\t\n507\tTable 4 measures every conversation against the\n508\ttask’s own reference workload, the ideal tool-call\n509\tcount in the enterprise worlds and the optimal block\n510\tcount in Pathfinding. In the enterprise worlds the\n511\tengaged systems fail by doing too much: they exceed the ideal workload in 50–83% of conversations, with over-effort ratios of 1.7–3.0, largest in\n512\tTravel, the world whose modal right answer is\n513\tto do nothing. The disengaged system fails the\n514\topposite way, falling short of the workload in 58–\n515\t\n516\t\fAgentic Capability\n517\tPass@3\n518\t\n519\tPass3\n520\t\n521\tTT\n522\t\n523\t0.415±.081 0.037±.033\n524\t0.585±.081 0.207±.067\n525\t0.689±.078 0.200±.070\n526\t2.1\n527\tmini 0.385±.081 0.126±.056\n528\tVTF 0.726±.074 0.326±.081\n529\t\n530\t0.037±.056\n531\t0.363±.161\n532\t0.352±.167\n533\t0.233±.141\n534\t0.511±.169\n535\t\n536\t0.037±.056\n537\t0.085±.094\n538\t0.063±.072\n539\t0.044±.061\n540\t0.144±.104\n541\t\n542\t0.760±.043\n543\t0.449±.033\n544\t0.763±.028\n545\t0.535±.051\n546\t0.686±.033\n547\t\n548\t0.052±.037 0.000±.000\n549\t0.630±.081 0.489±.085\n550\t0.637±.081 0.533±.081\n551\t2.1\n552\tmini 0.333±.081 0.296±.078\n553\tVTF 0.652±.081 0.519±.081\n554\t\n555\t0.000±.000\n556\t0.715±.150\n557\t0.704±.150\n558\t0.474±.159\n559\t0.685±.159\n560\t\n561\t0.000±.000\n562\t0.270±.150\n563\t0.381±.170\n564\t0.152±.120\n565\t0.341±.154\n566\t\n567\t0.385±.081 0.007±.011\n568\t0.652±.078 0.