{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9f53d5d530337407", "type": "tool_result", "content": "1400\tXiao, Zihan Zhang, Hui Bu, Xin Xu, Xinsheng\n1401\tWang, Hexin Liu, Eng Siong Chng, Hung-yi Lee,\n1402\tHaizhou Li, and Lei Xie. 2026. The ICASSP 2026\n1403\tHumDial challenge: Benchmarking human-like spoken dialogue systems in the LLM era. Preprint,\n1404\tarXiv:2601.05564.\n1405\t\n1406\tA\n1407\t\n1408\tNomenclature\n1409\t\n1410\tB\n1411\t\n1412\tHarness implementation\n1413\t\n1414\tOur harness follows the tick-based design established by τ -Voice and τ 2 -bench (Ray et al., 2026;\n1415\tBarres et al., 2025), and we build directly on their\n1416\treleased orchestrator rather than reimplementing it.\n1417\tSimulated time advances in 200 ms ticks, so model\n1418\t\n1419\t\flatency never shifts an event’s position in the timeline and a slow model and a fast model produce\n1420\tcomparable traces; each side hears the previous\n1421\ttick, and tool results deliver on the next tick so audio never stalls on tool latency. Task and evaluation\n1422\tscaffolding, the record-store abstraction, goal-state\n1423\tgrading and Passk are inherited from τ 2 -bench;\n1424\tfrom EVA-Bench we port the turn-taking metric\n1425\tverbatim, including its unanswered-turn rule, and\n1426\tadopt its practice of measuring user-simulator goal\n1427\tadherence without letting it gate reward (Bogavelli\n1428\tet al., 2026). Building on a shared harness is deliberate: it holds the measurement apparatus fixed\n1429\twhile the questions change.\n1430\tOur own additions are confined to five places: a\n1431\tsilence and suspension sentinel that makes dead air\n1432\tscorable in the SUSPENSION type; bipartite goldaction matching (presence only, so an omission\n1433\tfails while surplus does not) for POLICY REFUSAL;\n1434\tdistractor injection with gold labels written at injection time, which is what makes selectivity scorable\n1435\tagainst ground truth; a voice preflight that screens\n1436\tevery persona against the server VAD threshold\n1437\tbefore any scored run, which Section I shows is\n1438\tnot optional; and an annotation layer over the tick\n1439\tstream that attributes anomalous runs to agent, simulator or harness before scoring. Of the eleven\n1440\tconversation types only two require any of these\n1441\tto be scorable at all, and the two Pathfinding types\n1442\tneeded a new world rather than a harness change.\n1443\tThe harness is infrastructure for this work rather\n1444\tthan a contribution of it.\n1445\tInfrastructure failure means rerun and never\n1446\tscore; agent non-response is a valid scored end\n1447\tstate, and agent freeze is a hard zero on TT through\n1448\tthe unanswered-turn term. Credentials are matched\n1449\ton their spoken renderings, so “three four five” and\n1450\t“345” are one value. One provider-side artefact is\n1451\thandled at this layer: Nova 2 Sonic’s Pathfinding sessions are terminated by the provider’s own\n1452\tsession cap (Appendix E.1).\n1453\t\n1454\tC\n1455\t\n1456\tSystems and configuration\n1457\t\n1458\tAll five systems are served over WebSocket realtime endpoints through one adapter. llm_args is\n1459\tnull on every scored run: no generation parameters are set anywhere, so every system runs at\n1460\tprovider defaults. No vendor returns a dated snapshot identifier through the client, so the strings\n1461\tof Table 2 are the family identifiers the APIs report. Pathfinding access windows, first-to-last\n1462\t\n1463\trole\n1464\t\n1465\tmodel\n1466\t\n1467\tnotes\n1468\t\n1469\tuser simulator\n1470\t\n1471\tgpt-5.6-luna\n1472\t(Azure)\n1473\t\n1474\twrites the caller’s\n1475\tor walker’s words;\n1476\tprovider-default\n1477\tsampling\n1478\t“should I interrupt”\n1479\tand “should I\n1480\tbackchannel” as\n1481\ttwo independent\n1482\tbinary calls every\n1483\t∼2.0 s while the\n1484\tagent speaks;\n1485\trealistic channel\n1486\tonly\n1487\tTable 12,\n1488\tAppendix H\n1489\t\n1490\tdecision model claude-haiku-4.5\n1491\t(OpenRouter)\n1492\t\n1493\tjudges\n1494\t\n1495\tper metric\n1496\t\n1497\tTable 6: Harness-side models, uniform across every\n1498\tworld and every reported number. Turn-taking control\n1499\tsits entirely on the user side; the agent under test is\n1500\tnever told any threshold.\n1501\t\n1502\tscored run: gpt-realtime-2.1 2026-07-30 to 0803, gpt-realtime-2.1-mini 2026-07-31 to 0803, gemini-3.1-flash-live-preview 2026-0801 to 08-03, xai-realtime 2026-08-01 to 08-03,\n1503\tamazon.nova-2-sonic-v1:0 2026-08-02. The\n1504\tmatched configuration across all six worlds: speech\n1505\tcomplexity regular, step cap 1200 s, wall-clock\n1506\ttimeout 1200 s, server VAD threshold 0.2, fixed\n1507\tseed, persona pinned per scenario (Appendix G).\n1508\t\n1509\tD\n1510\t\n1511\tWorld specifications: enterprise worlds\n1512\t\n1513\tEach enterprise world is one instantiation of the\n1514\ttelephone-support construct of Section 3.1; Table 7\n1515\tgives the per-world regimes and Table 8 the conversation types. The unsafe behaviour in several\n1516\tregimes is unrepresentable rather than discouraged,\n1517\tbecause it is enforced in the tool surface: Banking\n1518\tcontains no tool that would require an employee\n1519\tto hear a one-time code aloud, Healthcare gates\n1520\tclaim reads on the verified member so that authority\n1521\tis decided per record, and Travel scores restraint\n1522\tthrough negative assertions and write-counting\n1523\trather than end-state checks. Each scenario names\n1524\tits reward basis B(x) ⊆ {GS, ACT, NLA}, and\n1525\tthe per-scenario bases, together with the difficultygoverning parameters that live inside a type (escalation count, candidate-record count, interruption\n1526\tcount), ship with the release.\n1527\tAll six worlds share one volatility stressor: the\n1528\tworld can change with no notification, discoverably\n1529\tonly by re-querying. This exposes three sources\n1530\tof divergence between what the agent believes and\n1531\t\n1532\t\fworld\n1533\t\n1534\tgoverning regime\n1535\t\n1536\tauthority\n1537\tgranularity\n1538\t\n1539\trefusal\n1540\tcharacter\n1541\t\n1542\twhat it isolates\n1543\t\n1544\tBanking\n1545\t\n1546\tfinancial-crime\n1547\tstatute\n1548\t\n1549\tper caller, stepped\n1550\tup by operation\n1551\trisk tier\n1552\t\n1553\tstatutory\n1554\t\n1555\tLogistics\n1556\t\n1557\tcontract topology\n1558\tover physical goods\n1559\t\n1560\tper the shipment’s\n1561\tcontractual parties\n1562\t\n1563\tcontractual,\n1564\tphysical\n1565\t\n1566\tHealthcare\n1567\t\n1568\tlawful disclosure\n1569\t\n1570\tper record, via a\n1571\tdisclosure matrix\n1572\t\n1573\tprivacy\n1574\t\n1575\tper policyholder\n1576\t\n1577\tinstitutional\n1578\t\n1579\tTranslating a symptom into an operation\n1580\twhen several plausible, sympathetically\n1581\tframed requests are reporting-threshold\n1582\ttripwires.\n1583\tDeciding who is entitled to redirect goods\n1584\tthe agent can move in the record but cannot\n1585\tsee.\n1586\tRefusing without leaking in the act of\n1587\trefusing. A fully verified caller may be\n1588\tentitled to nothing.\n1589\tTaking first notice of a loss the agent is\n1590\tstructurally forbidden from deciding.\n1591\t\n1592\tper delegate list\n1593\tand co-host roster\n1594\t\n1595\tscope\n1596\t\n1597\t−\n1598\t\n1599\t−\n1600\t\n1601\tInsurance\n1602\t\n1603\tinstitutional rules\n1604\tforbidding\n1605\tadjudication\n1606\tTravel\n1607\tthe platform’s own\n1608\tlimited remit\n1609\tbetween two parties\n1610\tPathfinding perceptual\n1611\tgrounding\n1612\t\n1613\tDoing nothing, correctly: the modal right\n1614\tanswer is a factual correction or a refusal\n1615\theld with nowhere to escalate to.\n1616\tGrounding an instruction against a heading\n1617\tneither party can state.\n1618\t\n1619\tTable 7: The six regimes: what governs each world, at what granularity authority is decided, what refusal looks like\n1620\tthere, and the capability each isolates.\n1621\t\n1622\twhat is true, and each world instantiates all three:\n1623\tthe world changes (a record moves mid-call; a closure appears on the planned route), the user’s intent\n1624\tchanges (a premise is revised; a second destination surfaces), or the user’s execution diverges (the\n1625\tcaller misacts on an instruction; the walker takes\n1626\tthe wrong turn). The three demand different repairs, and prior interruption work varies only the\n1627\tsecond (Lin et al., 2026a; Modi et al., 2026; Salimi\n1628\tet al., 2026).\n1629\t\n1630\tE\n1631\t\n1632\tWorld specifications: Pathfinding\n1633\t\n1634\tWorld. An 8 × 8 rectilinear grid: 64 junctions\n1635\tand 105 walkable segments, with two superblocks\n1636\tremoving 7 edges so that naive rectilinear reasoning fails. Block spacing is uniform (274 m avenue,\n1637\t81 m street) and time advances in 200 ms ticks to a\n1638\t6,000-tick cap, twenty simulated minutes. The paper’s type names map to the release as SINGLE IN TENT = base (five blocks, two turns, no closures),\n1639\tREROUTING = blocked (four closures absent from\n1640\tthe copilot’s map seal every visible route; exactly\n1641\tone seven-block route survives), and ALL - DAY AS SISTANCE = errand (two legs of 5 + 6 blocks, the\n1642\tsecond stop revealed only on arrival at the first).\n1643\tTool surface. Walker motion is maneuver-driven:\n1644\tone maneuver call moves one street corner, and\n1645\tthe walker keeps talking while moving. Nine\n1646\twalker-side maneuvers (turns, walking, crossing,\n1647\tsign-reading, looking around) are paired with five\n1648\t\n1649\tcopilot-side reads (GPS, place lookup, directions,\n1650\tlive status, and a write-only belief probe). All returns are natural-language strings rather than structured schemas: GPS is described as accurate to\n1651\tabout 40 metres and never includes heading, and\n1652\tlive status reports closures only within two blocks\n1653\tof the walker, so querying early returns nothing and\n1654\ta belief formed from a tool result expires silently.\n1655\tThe heading constraint. Heading is ground truth\n1656\tin the environment and never exposed: no walker\n1657\ttool returns it, and the directions call takes no facing argument and returns absolute bearings. The\n1658\twalker’s refusal of compass words is enforced by\n1659\tprompt only, so the constraint is structural on the\n1660\ttool surface and prompt-level on the persona; in\n1661\t68% of REROUTING calls the copilot still asks a\n1662\tvariant of “which way is north”, and the walker’s\n1663\trefusal is what holds.\n1664\tArrival scoring. Scoring is a single post-hoc environment assertion, deliberately not exposed as a\n1665\tcallable tool. It requires the walker to be standing\n1666\tat the destination node when the call ends rather\n1667\tthan merely to have passed through it; latching on\n1668\tfirst touch was rejected after a probe conversation\n1669\tscored 1.0 for a walker led eight blocks past the\n1670\tgoal.\n1671\tExploration share. The exploration share of Table 14 is the fraction of walker moves made under\n1672\tuncertainty rather than on a confident instruction,\n1673\tlabelled per move by gpt-5.6-luna over the tick\n1674\t\n1675\t\ftype\n1676\t\n1677\tthe shape it fixes, and what it tests\n1678\t\n1679\tOne request, one resolution path. The\n1680\tcontrol condition; in Pathfinding, a\n1681\tbase route of five blocks and two turns.\n1682\tMULTI\n1683\tSeveral requests, resolvable in more\n1684\tINTENT\n1685\tthan one order, with at least one\n1686\tdependency: goal decomposition under\n1687\ta live conversation.\n1688\tPOLICY\n1689\tA well-formed request that must be\n1690\tREFUSAL\n1691\trefused. Correctness is a property of\n1692\twhat is withheld.\n1693\tRECORD DIS - More than one record matches what the\n1694\tAMBIGUATION\n1695\tcaller said; acting before\n1696\tdisambiguating is the failure.\n1697\tIDENTITY\n1698\tAuthority must be established before\n1699\tVERIFICATION\n1700\tanything is read or written, and a failed\n1701\tcheck must not leak the record’s\n1702\texistence.\n1703\tGUIDED\n1704\tThe effectors move to the user: the\n1705\tPROCEDURE\n1706\tagent instructs, waits, and must trust an\n1707\tunverifiable human report as the trigger\n1708\tfor its own write.\n1709\tMID - CALL\n1710\tThe caller revises a premise after the\n1711\tCORRECTION\n1712\tagent has begun acting on it.\n1713\tSUSPENSION\n1714\tThe call is interrupted and resumed\n1715\tacross a gap the agent must hold state\n1716\tover; the one type in which dead air is\n1717\titself scored.\n1718\tNARRATIVE\n1719\tA long unstructured account from\n1720\tINTAKE\n1721\twhich the agent must extract, confirm\n1722\tand file the structured facts.\n1723\tSINGLE\n1724\tINTENT\n1725\t\n1726\tREROUTING\n1727\t\n1728\tALL - DAY\n1729\tASSISTANCE\n1730\t\n1731\tClosures missing from the map seal\n1732\tevery visible route; querying early\n1733\treturns nothing, so a belief formed from\n1734\ta tool result expires silently. Arises only\n1735\tin Pathfinding.\n1736\tA second goal emerges on arrival at the\n1737\tfirst; the test is staying with the user,\n1738\tand useful, over a long horizon. Arises\n1739\tonly in Pathfinding.\n1740\t\n1741\tTable 8: The eleven conversation types. Types 1–9 are\n1742\tshared by the five enterprise worlds; the last two arise\n1743\tonly in Pathfinding, whose episodes are all structurally\n1744\tGUIDED PROCEDURE with one of SINGLE INTENT ,\n1745\tREROUTING or ALL - DAY ASSISTANCE layered on top\n1746\t(release names base, blocked, errand; Appendix D).\n1747\t\n1748\tstream; all 30 condition–channel cells are labelled.\n1749\tThe replay also computes a heading-localisation\n1750\ttrace per run: position is essentially solved by every\n1751\tsystem (accuracy 0.93–1.00) while heading is not\n1752\t(0.22–0.93), and the gap is dominated by omission\n1753\trather than by wrong assertions.\n1754\tReleased, uncampaigned variants. Four authored variants are