{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-abb8d2da1b1f0d01", "type": "tool_result", "content": "2400\tOne caveat accompanies the cell: Nova 2 Sonic’s\n2401\tPathfinding sessions are additionally censored by\n2402\tits provider’s own session cap (Appendix E.1).\n2403\t\n2404\t\fReaching the right state is not doing the task.\n2405\tAcross the 25 enterprise cells the mean of GS −\n2406\tPass@1 is +0.255, and every cell is positive:\n2407\tlargest in Banking (+0.381 on average, up to\n2408\t+0.489) and smallest in Logistics (+0.093). The\n2409\tremaining conjuncts, acting through the sanctioned\n2410\tsequence and saying what was done, are where\n2411\tthe reward is lost (Tables 13 and 18 decompose\n2412\tthem). A do-nothing agent passes GS wherever\n2413\tthe gold terminal state equals the seeded state, and\n2414\tNova 2 Sonic makes this visible: gold state in\n2415\t34.1–41.5% of conversations in four worlds while\n2416\tissuing no adequate tool call in most, against 5.2%\n2417\tin Logistics, the world with the least to refuse.\n2418\tGS is a capability measure only conditioned on the\n2419\tworld containing something to change, and a benchmark that headlines goal state is partly reporting\n2420\thow many of its tasks are no-ops.\n2421\tWhy accuracy and experience trade off. The\n2422\tsystems that call tools most have the worst turntaking: Gemini-3.1-Flash-Live falls short of the\n2423\treference workload in 10% and 3% of Logistics\n2424\tand Travel conversations and scores 0.443 and\n2425\t0.314 on TT, the worst in both, while Nova 2\n2426\tSonic falls short in 77% and 64% and scores 0.631\n2427\tand 0.695. Tool calls introduce silence, silence\n2428\tis scored as a timing failure, and any composite\n2429\tthat gates on timing penalises acting. This gives a\n2430\tmechanism for EVA-Bench’s finding that no system exceeds 0.5 on both accuracy and experience\n2431\t(Bogavelli et al., 2026).\n2432\tHow much of the score is the harness? Three\n2433\tconfiguration dials, none of which any published\n2434\tvoice benchmark reports, move scores by as much\n2435\tas the choice of system does (Appendix L). At\n2436\tthe default 0.5 server-VAD threshold, some synthesised personas are effectively inaudible: one\n2437\ttriggered the agent in 0 of 27 sessions, another\n2438\tpassed 1 of 77 runs, and the agent greeted and then\n2439\tfell silent in 67 of 128 simulations; at 0.2 the effect\n2440\tlargely disappears. A benchmark pairing synthetic\n2441\tpersonas with a default VAD threshold is partly\n2442\tmeasuring persona loudness, and the resulting silence is indistinguishable from an agent that chose\n2443\tnot to speak. Holding the agent fixed, the choice of\n2444\tuser-simulator model moves Pass@1 from 0.267 to\n2445\t0.578 (Table 10), while the MOS predictors barely\n2446\tmove, consistent with their measuring the agent’s\n2447\taudio rather than the interaction. And the step cap\n2448\tforce-zeroes runs that do not terminate: excluding\n2449\tcapped runs moves one system’s pooled score from\n2450\t\n2451\t0.383 to 0.469 and another’s from 0.108 to 0.213,\n2452\tnarrowing a reported 3.5× system gap to 2.2×.\n2453\tInside Pathfinding: the mechanisms bite.\n2454\tREROUTING costs every system most of its reward.\n2455\tNo system exceeds Pass@1 of 0.27 in either channel, against up to 0.80 on SINGLE INTENT, while\n2456\tthe acoustic channel moves Pass@1 far less than\n2457\tthe geometry does, and in no consistent direction\n2458\t( Gemini-3.1-Flash-Live rises from 0.13 to 0.27\n2459\tunder realistic acoustics on REROUTING; Grok\n2460\tVoice Think Fast 1.0 falls from 0.27 to 0.13). ALL DAY ASSISTANCE sits between, and only the systems that survive REROUTING recover on it. The\n2461\treward’s operating point matters less than it might:\n2462\tmoving the efficiency threshold η0 across [0.5, 1.0]\n2463\tmoves levels far more than ranks, the one rank\n2464\tevent being a 0.044 swap between the top two at\n2465\tthe operating point itself (Table 9, Appendix E).\n2466\tExploration separates systems, not conditions.\n2467\tThe exploration share is this world’s betweensystem marker: 16.2% of Gemini-3.1-FlashLive’s walker moves (move-weighted) and 22.7%\n2468\tof Grok Voice Think Fast 1.0’s are made under\n2469\tuncertainty rather than on a confident instruction,\n2470\tagainst 40.3% for GPT-Realtime-2.1-mini, 43.4%\n2471\tfor GPT-Realtime-2.1 and 51.2% for Nova 2\n2472\tSonic, and across the five systems it tracks the reward at ρ = −0.80. Within a system, moving to a\n2473\tharder condition does not raise it consistently, so\n2474\tit marks systems rather than conditions, and we\n2475\tmake no causal claim. It gives the efficiency story\n2476\tits mechanism: GPT-Realtime-2.1 is efficient and\n2477\tstill lost (ϱ+ of 1.48 over 40% of conversations, below its own five-world range, with GS 0.400 also\n2478\tbelow), while Nova 2 Sonic wanders (ϱ+ of 4.25,\n2479\ton a conditioning population of eight conversations). Efficient-and-lost and inefficient-and-lost\n2480\tare different failures, and the exploration share separates them where the reward alone cannot. Almost\n2481\tnone of these failures is a wrong destination: on\n2482\tthe realistic channel, 104 of 110 non-arrivals end\n2483\tat the step cap and only six end at the wrong place\n2484\t(Appendix E.1). Nobody gets lost; they run out of\n2485\ttime.\n2486\t\n2487\tJ\n2488\t\n2489\tRange analysis\n2490\t\n2491\tTable 15 reads every Pathfinding value against the\n2492\tinterval the same system spans across the five enterprise worlds: 15 of the 20 cells on the four identicalcode metrics leave that interval, no Pass@1 cell\n2493\t\n2494\t\fidentical code\n2495\tTT\n2496\t\n2497\tsystem\n2498\t\n2499\tCP\n2500\t\n2501\tSEL\n2502\t\n2503\tanalogue\n2504\tFAI\n2505\t\n2506\tGS\n2507\t\n2508\t2 Sonic\n2509\t0.062⇓ 1.022 0.991 1.244⇓ 0.000⇓\n2510\t3.1-Flash-Live\n2511\t0.538⇑ 1.178⇓ 0.782⇑ 1.511 0.978⇑\n2512\tRealtime-2.